{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And you shall do what is right and good in the eyes of HaShem.</b> By way of the plain sense, it says: you shall observe the commandments of HaShem, His testimonies and His statutes, and in their performance you shall intend to do only what is good and right in His eyes. And 'that it may go well with you' is a promise, meaning: for when you do what is good in His eyes, it will go well with you, for HaShem brings good to those who are good and upright in their hearts. But our Rabbis had a fine midrash on this, saying: this is compromise and going beyond the line of the law. The intention here is that first it said that you shall observe His statutes and testimonies which He has commanded you, and now it says: even regarding that which He did not command you, give your mind to do what is good and right in His eyes, for He loves the good and the right. And this is a great matter, for it is impossible for the Torah to mention all of a person's conduct toward his neighbors and friends, and all of his business dealings, and the ordinances of settled life and of states in their entirety. But after having mentioned many of them — such as 'You shall not go about as a talebearer' (Leviticus 19:16), 'You shall not take vengeance nor bear a grudge' (ibid. verse 18), 'Neither shall you stand idly by the blood of your neighbor' (ibid. verse 16), 'You shall not curse the deaf' (ibid. verse 14), 'You shall rise before the hoary head' (ibid. verse 32), and similar ones — it returned to say by way of a general principle that one should do what is good and right in every matter, so that this includes compromise and going beyond the line of the law, such as what they mentioned concerning the law of the bar metzra (Bava Metzia 108a), and even what they said (Yoma 86a): 'One's manner of speaking should be pleasant with people gently,' so that he is called in every respect wholehearted and upright:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:22.261247297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}